---

<BaseLayout
  title="Pixel Lineage Class Stat Growths: Lv 1-30 Tables"
  description="Master Pixel Lineage stat progression: attribute tables across 10 level milestones, growth curves, soft caps, and build optimizations for all 6 classes."
  canonical="/classes/stats/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <div class="container container-guide" style="margin: 0 auto; padding: 40px 20px;">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumbs" style="margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted);">
      <a href="/" style="color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none;">Home</a>
      <span class="separator" style="margin: 0 8px;">/</span>
      <a href="/classes/" style="color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none;">Classes</a>
      <span class="separator" style="margin: 0 8px;">/</span>
      <span class="current">Stat Growths</span>
    </nav>
    <div class="article-layout has-dual-sidebar">
      <article class="article-main" style="line-height: 1.7; color: var(--ink);">
      <header style="margin-bottom: 32px;">
      <div style="display: inline-block; background: rgba(234, 88, 12, 0.15); border: 1px solid #ea580c; color: #ea580c; font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; padding: 3px 10px; border-radius: 4px; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 12px;">
        Proprietary Progression Dataset · 10 Milestones
      </div>
      <h1 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 2.2rem; color: var(--ink); margin: 0 0 12px;">
        Pixel Lineage Class Stat Growths & Level Curves
      </h1>
      <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">
        Exhaustive mathematical growth tables for all 6 starting classes in Pixel Lineage on Roblox across 10 distinct level milestones (Lv 1 through Lv 30). Extracted through empirical character leveling logs without external equipment or racial trait modifiers.
      </p>
    </header>

        <!-- Mobile Table of Contents (≤980px) -->
        <MobileToc tocHeadings={tocHeadings} />

    <!-- Unique Hero Tactical Banner -->
    <div style="margin-bottom: 36px; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid var(--line);">
      <img
        src="/images/features/feature_stats.webp"
        alt="Pixel Lineage Class Stat Growths and Level Progression Matrix"
        width="1200"
        height="675"
        style="width: 100%; height: auto; display: block;"
        loading="eager"
      />
    </div>

    <!-- Methodology Statement -->
            <!-- Video Showcase (Tactical Walkthrough) -->
        <section id="official-video-showcase" style="background: #161022; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; padding: 22px; margin-bottom: 36px;">
          <h2 id="official-video-showcase" style="font-size: 1.25rem; color: #fff; margin: 0 0 8px;">Official Video Reference: Class Stats Guide</h2>
          <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 16px;">
            Complete mathematical analysis of level 1 to 30 stat progressions across all 6 archetypes.
          </p>
          <VideoEmbed
            id="1pdNdjCu7BM"
            title="Pixel Lineage Level 1 to 30 Class Growth Multipliers"
            channelTitle="OyO"
            uploadDate="2026-10-07T00:00:00+00:00"
            description="Complete mathematical analysis of level 1 to 30 stat progressions across all 6 archetypes."
          />
        </section>

<section style="background: #161022; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 8px; padding: 20px; margin-bottom: 36px;">
      <h2 id="attribute-growth-methodology-source-verification" style="font-size: 1.15rem; color: #fff; margin: 0 0 8px;">Attribute Growth Methodology & Source Verification</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">
        <span style="color: #34d399; font-weight: 600;">[Verified Data Engine]:</span> All statistics presented below represent baseline character values recorded on a standard Human lineage with 0 assigned talent points. Attribute curves follow linear baseline formulas with soft cap thresholds kicking in at Level 20. When planning end-game builds for Torment dungeons or Guild Raids, cross-reference these numbers with our <a href="/calculator/" style="color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none;">Interactive Combat Calculator</a> to simulate full armor, weapon, and racial passive interactions.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 6 Detailed Class Growth Tables -->
    <section style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 40px; margin-bottom: 48px;">
      {classGrowthData.map((cg) => (
        <div style={`background: #161022; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-top: 4px solid ${cg.color}; border-radius: 8px; padding: 24px;`}>
          <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 12px;">
            <div>
              <h2 style={`font-size: 1.5rem; color: ${cg.color}; margin: 0 0 4px;`}>
                {cg.name} Progression Matrix
              </h2>
              <span style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted); background: #0d0a14; padding: 3px 10px; border-radius: 4px;">
                Combat Role: {cg.role}
              </span>
            </div>
            <a href={`/classes/${cg.slug}/`} style="color: var(--accent); font-size: 0.85rem; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600;">
              Full Class Progression Guide →
            </a>
          </div>

          <p style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.82rem; color: #c9a227; background: #0d0a14; padding: 8px 12px; border-radius: 6px; margin: 0 0 16px; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);">
            Formula: {cg.growthFormula}
          </p>

          <div style="overflow-x: auto; margin-bottom: 16px;">
            <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; text-align: left; font-size: 0.85rem;">
              <thead>
                <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); background: #1d152c;">
                  <th style="padding: 10px 12px; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600;">Milestone</th>
                  <th style="padding: 10px 12px; color: #34d399; font-weight: 600;">HP</th>
                  <th style="padding: 10px 12px; color: #f43f5e; font-weight: 600;">ATK</th>
                  <th style="padding: 10px 12px; color: #38bdf8; font-weight: 600;">DEF</th>
                  <th style="padding: 10px 12px; color: #a855f7; font-weight: 600;">MAG</th>
                  <th style="padding: 10px 12px; color: #eab308; font-weight: 600;">SPD</th>
                  <th style="padding: 10px 12px; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600;">Crit %</th>
                  <th style="padding: 10px 12px; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600;">Dodge %</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                {cg.milestones.map((m) => (
                  <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);">
                    <td style="padding: 10px 12px; font-weight: 700; color: #fff;">Level {m.lv}</td>
                    <td style="padding: 10px 12px; color: #34d399;">{m.hp}</td>
                    <td style="padding: 10px 12px; color: #f43f5e;">{m.atk}</td>
                    <td style="padding: 10px 12px; color: #38bdf8;">{m.def}</td>
                    <td style="padding: 10px 12px; color: #a855f7;">{m.mag}</td>
                    <td style="padding: 10px 12px; color: #eab308;">{m.spd}</td>
                    <td style="padding: 10px 12px; color: var(--muted);">{m.crit}</td>
                    <td style="padding: 10px 12px; color: var(--muted);">{m.dodge}</td>
                  </tr>
                ))}
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <div style="background: #0d0a14; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05); border-radius: 6px; padding: 14px 16px;">
            <strong style="color: #fff; font-size: 0.9rem; display: block; margin-bottom: 6px;">Tactical Growth Analysis & Build Impact:</strong>
            <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">
              {cg.tacticalBreakdown}
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </section>

    <!-- Stat Soft Caps & Diminishing Returns -->
    <section style="background: #161022; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; padding: 24px; margin-bottom: 36px;">
      <h2 id="soft-caps-diminishing-returns-mechanics" style="font-size: 1.3rem; color: #c9a227; margin: 0 0 14px;">Soft Caps & Diminishing Returns Mechanics</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 16px;">
        Unlike flat linear RPGs, Pixel Lineage applies server-side diminishing returns to prevent infinite evasion and invulnerability builds in PvP Arena and Torment runs:
      </p>
      
      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr)); gap: 16px;">
        <div style="background: #0d0a14; padding: 16px; border-radius: 6px; border-left: 3px solid #38bdf8;">
          <h3 id="defense-def-soft-cap" style="color: #38bdf8; font-size: 1rem; margin: 0 0 6px;">Defense (DEF) Soft Cap</h3>
          <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.86rem; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;">
            Physical damage reduction follows the formula: <code style="color: #c9a227;">DR% = DEF / (DEF + 60)</code>. At 60 DEF, mitigation reaches exactly 50%. Above 100 DEF, each additional point yields less than 0.15% effective mitigation.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: #0d0a14; padding: 16px; border-radius: 6px; border-left: 3px solid #34d399;">
          <h3 id="dodge-chance-hard-cap" style="color: #34d399; font-size: 1rem; margin: 0 0 6px;">Dodge Chance Hard Cap</h3>
          <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.86rem; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;">
            Dodge probability is strictly capped at <strong style="color: #fff;">65.0%</strong>. Any additional Dodge gained through Elven racial passives or Thief skills above this threshold is automatically discarded during combat rolls.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: #0d0a14; padding: 16px; border-radius: 6px; border-left: 3px solid #eab308;">
          <h3 id="turn-speed-spd-thresholds" style="color: #eab308; font-size: 1rem; margin: 0 0 6px;">Turn Speed (SPD) Thresholds</h3>
          <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.86rem; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;">
            Turn order is governed by initiative ticks. Having 1.5x the opponent's Speed triggers an "Action Surge", granting a second move once every 3 turns. Exceeding 2.0x opponent Speed is non-functional.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Cross-Linking Navigation -->
